  "body": "**Replaces #437** (opened from the old fork, which cannot take pushes). The parents #516 (#416) and #517 (#417) are merged on main. This PR now holds only the #418 work.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n- **The option:** `ThreadInfeed.repeat_each_depth`, off by default. Each pass above the root is followed by an identical copy: the same tip depth, the same lattice shift, the same helix phase. Thus a repeat cannot cut deeper and cannot move. The finishing pass and the spring passes at the root are not repeated.\r\n- **Alternating infeed:** the side flips one time for each depth, not for each cut. Thus a repeat keeps its flank.\r\n- **G76 refuses it by name, on the two lathe posts.** The record carries a `repeat_each_depth` flag. The stream writes it as `REP 1` only when it is set. The post property is `RepeatEachDepth`.\r\n  - `fanuc-lathe.cps` refuses with \"repeat each roughing depth is not a G76 cycle (the cycle cuts each depth once)\".\r\n  - `tormach-lathe.cps` (added in the takeover, 2026-11-15) refuses with \"G76 threading cycle refused - repeat each roughing depth - LinuxCNC's G76 cuts each depth once\". Before this change, the PathPilot G76 ignored the flag and posted a cycle that cuts each depth one time, which is not the verified passes.\r\n  - G32 / G33 passes post the repeat.\r\n- **Defaults are byte-identical:** the stamp adds one byte only when the flag is on. No project key and no stream word is written when it is off. No version rung. No golden changed.\r\n- **UI:** a \"Repeat each depth\" checkbox on the Passes tab, after Spring passes. Its tooltip says G32 only, says that G76 refuses it, and says that tooling makers recommend against routine spring passes.\r\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/418-thread-repeat-pass.md` (with the Tormach entry).\r\n\r\n## Readings (motion `turning_thread_infeed`, plunge depths in mm, 1.2 mm thread height)\r\n- Repeat on, no finish allowance: 0.4, 0.4, 0.8, 0.8, 1.2 (the root pass is the finishing pass, cut one time).\r\n- Repeat on, finish allowance 0.1, one spring pass: 0.4, 0.4, 0.8, 0.8, 1.1, 1.1, 1.2, 1.2 (finishing pass 1.2, then the spring pass 1.2; neither is repeated).\r\n- Repeat off: the moves are identical to the plan without the flag.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n- motion `turning_thread_infeed`:\r\n  - each roughing depth is cut two times, and the default is unchanged move for move;\r\n  - a repeat is the same pass under each method and schedule, and the verdict stays silent.\r\n- app `turning_thread_infeed`: the toggle goes stale and back to OK, takes 3 then 5 plunges, with undo and redo. The project round-trip writes the key only when it is set.\r\n- app `lathe_post_g76_schedule`: Fanuc G76 refuses the repeat; `REP 1` is in the stream; G32 posts 5 passes.\r\n- app `lathe_post_tormach_thread::a_g76_record_the_cycle_cannot_state_exactly_is_refused_by_name`: new case \"repeat each roughing depth\" (PathPilot G76 refuses, no `G76 P` written).\r\n\r\n## Gate (takeover head, after the merge of main `a1ef0219e`)\r\nAll green, on head `a9c44916a`, no edits during the run:\r\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only cl --only post`: cl 3 binaries, 49 passed; post 57 binaries, 518 passed; 0 failed.\r\n- motion: lib 366 passed (5 ignored), `turning_thread` 18, `turning_thread_cycle` 3, `turning_thread_infeed` 10.\r\n- app: lib 313 (1 ignored), `lathe_post_tormach_thread` 8, `lathe_post_tormach` 8, `lathe_post_g76` 8, `lathe_post_g76_schedule` 7, `lathe_post_inch` 6, `lathe_post` 7, `lathe_post_css` 10, `lathe_thread_travel` 2, `turning_thread` 10, `turning_thread_infeed` 5, `tormach_lathes` 2, `project_roundtrip` 73, `conformance` 7, `golden_cl` 33, `posting` 17, `recorded_post_streams` 5, `coarse_laws` 6.\r\n- ui: lib `thread` filter, 6 passed.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n- No GUI check of the new row on this head (the screenshots below are from the author's earlier head).\r\n- No lathe simulation run and no controller or machine run of a repeat program. The G32 / G33 output with the repeat has had no controller run. The two G76 refusals are pinned by tests only.\r\n- The headless-GPU ui tests and the release-tier heavy lanes were not run.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Threading op: optional repeat of each roughing depth (G32 / G33 output; the Fanuc and PathPilot G76 cycles refuse it by name) (#418)\r\n\r\n## Screenshots (Passes tab)\r\n\r\nRendered headless (egui_kittest `Harness::render()` on lavapipe) through the real `pages::properties` code: a lathe, bar stock, the TD-1732-60 threading insert and one Threading op, Passes tab open. Before is upstream/main of that time, so the after-shot also shows the rows of the stacked parents (#516 infeed plan, now on main). After: Flank 29.5°, Constant area, minimum depth 0.05 mm, finish allowance 0.03 mm, 1 spring pass, with **Repeat each depth** on - the new row of this PR.\r\n\r\n| Before (upstream/main) | After (this PR) |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-518/passes-tab-before.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/screenshots/pr-518/passes-tab-after.png) |\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\nMCP follow-up: #1847\r\n\r\nFixes #418\r\n",
